# Your zsh configuration.
#
# Tundra's own settings — prompt, history, completion, aliases — are already loaded from
# /etc/zsh/zshrc.d/tundra.zsh before this file runs. This file is yours; it starts empty and
# stays empty unless you put something in it.
#
# Anything here overrides Tundra's defaults, because it is sourced last. To drop one of them,
# override it rather than editing the system file: a system update replaces that file and
# will not touch this one.
#
#   PROMPT='%~ $ '          a plainer prompt
#   unalias ipconfig        drop one of the transition aliases
#   alias vi=nvim           your own
